Proposed (15.5s): Use this skill when the user wants a third-party API's documentation turned into reusable, persistent knowledge for coding agents — a Claude Skill package (SKILL.md + references/ + evals/) installed under ~/.claude/skills. Trigger on any request to build, generate, or make a skill / 技能包 / SKILL.md for a platform, SDK, or open platform (Stripe, Resend, 飞书, 火山引擎/豆包, Kimi/Moonshot, 智谱, an internal Mintlify/OpenAPI docs site…), and equally when the user just hands over a developer-docs or API-reference URL and says things like "整理成 AI 能用的东西" / "做成技能包" / "以后让 agent 直接写对代码" / "我们的 agent 老把参数、model 名写错" — even if they never say the word "skill". Also trigger when they mention having a test API key for real verification, or want proof the skill beats no-skill. Do NOT trigger for: answering one API question, writing code against an API, summarizing docs for humans, building an MCP server, or tuning an existing skill's description.

