Proposed (13.8s): Use this skill to turn an API platform's developer documentation into a durable, installable Claude Skill package (SKILL.md + references/ + evals/) that teaches coding agents to call that platform correctly on the first try — verified against the live API and proven with a with-skill vs without-skill comparison.

Reach for it whenever someone points at a product's docs site, API reference, or OpenAPI spec and wants that knowledge packaged for future agent use: "做一个 XX 的 skill / 技能包", "生成 SKILL.md", "把这套 API 文档整理成 AI 能用的东西", "以后让 agent 直接写对代码", "我们的 agent 老写错参数/model 名", scoping to certain modules, verifying with a test key, or installing into ~/.claude/skills. The word "skill" need not appear — the giveaway is docs-in, reusable-agent-knowledge-out.

Not for: answering a single API question, writing app code against an API, summarizing docs for people, building an MCP server, or rewording an existing skill.

